      ],
      "ref": "bow",
      "design": "Exactly4 ancient wooden CROSSBOWS WITH BOLT. All have the IDENTICAL three-quarter TOP view, projectile head toward upper RIGHT and wooden stock butt toward lower LEFT, horizontal bow limbs extend upper left and upper right, same angle and dimensions. A single thick wooden bolt on each central rail; no curved handbows or arrow quivers. iron darkwood; weathered bronze darkwood; heavy gold/red; Silla gold/ivory repeating-crossbow with a modest wooden bolt magazine but SAME orientation and overall footprint. Ancient trigger, no modern gun parts."
    },
