      "ref": "book",
      "design": "Exactly7 traditional Korean cloth-bound military BOOKS, in first7 grid cells; final2 cells completely empty. Identical CLOSED book silhouette, three-quarter front/top view, spine on LEFT, bottom page edges visible below, top edge slopes slightly upward to RIGHT, NEVER mirrored. Same thickness and size. Covers in order: ivory-green taegeuk; deep blue gold dragon; indigo constellation chart; red crossed spears; dark blue golden astronomy; ivory-red charitable relief ledger; black-green northern relief ledger. Gold corner fittings grow richer by rarity. NO bamboo on these7 books."
    },
    {
      "key": "bamboo",
      "cols": 3,
      "rows": 1,
      "ids": [
        "bamboo",
        "gilt_bamboo",
        "formation_scroll"
      ],
      "ref": "book",
      "design": "Exactly3 genuine ancient BAMBOO SLIP SCROLLS, NOT paper or Western books. Each is the SAME horizontally UNROLLED panel of12 narrow vertical bamboo slats connected by2 horizontal dark silk cords. Rolled bundle at LEFT and RIGHT edges, tied slats clearly readable. Identical three-quarter TOP/front view, long upper edge slopes slightly upward to RIGHT, equal size. Plain light brown bamboo and black cords; honey bamboo with jade-green ties and modest gold; dark green/brown tactical bamboo with red-gold bindings. NO hardback book cover, NO paper pages, NO invented text."
    },
