      "design": "Exactly13 empty traditional Korean ROBES in first13 cells, final3 cells fully empty. STRICT ORTHOGRAPHIC FRONT, shoulders level, two sleeves symmetric same width, sash horizontal, whole hip/knee-length coat silhouette, equal height. NO side view, NO turned shoulders, NO back view. Worn shape without a person, NOT folded cloth. Preserve overlapping collar construction but camera exactly centered. Ordered: plain white robe; ivory silk; white crane motifs; tan quilted; royal blue battle robe; green/gold embroidered; coarse tan hemp; scholar green; navy Taoist; pure white silk; purple; red/gold brocade; ceremonial gold. Subtle cloth differences, same pose."
